a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.conditional_rounding","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"boundary":"This is a conditional expectation identity, not a claim that F_N equals the terminal gradient pointwise. Independence and the bound |u|≤1 are essential.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-conditional-rounding"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"scalar.conditional_rounding","kind":"claim","label":"Independent Gaussian rounding preserves the conditional mean","locator":"consequences.tex:107–115,162–170; rounding paragraph","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-consequences","statement":"For fixed 0<T<1,N with finite positive normalizers, define F_N=sgn(u(T,Y_N)+2 Φ_G(Z_{N+1})−1), with Z_{N+1} independent of the first N coordinates and |u|≤1. Then E[F_N|Z₁,…,Z_N]=u(T,Y_N). Its zero set has probability zero, so the value assigned by sign at zero is immaterial.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","id":"field:aa3d7f6bad404a6fe7f7dd58501fc19252ba801d7cd9742758a9e643b18ff014","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286